WEBVTT

00:19.106 --> 00:23.026
[HANGE] I never expected Floch
to take action this quickly.

00:23.106 --> 00:26.696
[MAGATH] If the Jaegerists
destroy the flying boat,

00:26.776 --> 00:29.066
our plan would be
dead in the water.

00:29.156 --> 00:31.986
So why haven't they
done it already?

00:32.076 --> 00:34.286
[HANGE]
Hard to say.

00:34.366 --> 00:36.576
If I had to guess,
they suspect we're alive,

00:36.666 --> 00:38.496
and maybe that we're
trying to stop Eren,

00:38.576 --> 00:40.916
but they're not entirely sure.

00:40.996 --> 00:43.376
They could blow it up
in a second if they wanted to,

00:43.456 --> 00:44.876
but they can't
build another one.

00:44.966 --> 00:46.416
Without the
Azumabito's knowledge,

00:46.506 --> 00:48.926
they would have to
start from scratch.

00:49.006 --> 00:51.136
They'll wanna use it
for themselves if they can,

00:51.216 --> 00:53.926
to make sure the mainland's
been wiped clean.

00:54.016 --> 00:56.346
Plus, there're Azumabito
ships here.

00:56.436 --> 00:58.056
That might be
their real objective:

00:58.136 --> 00:59.306
to capture a small fleet

00:59.396 --> 01:01.566
and the technicians
to keep it afloat.

01:01.646 --> 01:03.066
But regardless.

01:03.146 --> 01:05.396
The Jaegerists would readily
sacrifice that objective

01:05.486 --> 01:07.316
if they caught wind of us.

01:07.396 --> 01:11.406
They'll blow the flying boat to
bits the second we're spotted.

01:11.486 --> 01:13.236
We've got a few of the Nine,

01:13.326 --> 01:14.746
so our odds are
better than they'd be

01:14.826 --> 01:18.326
in a straight firefight.
But not good.

01:19.286 --> 01:21.876
[MAGATH] True. We'll just
have to make the best of it.

01:21.956 --> 01:23.706
Fighting the Founder'll
be even worse.

01:23.796 --> 01:24.546
[Gasps]

01:24.626 --> 01:26.586
We'd better plan to--

01:36.966 --> 01:41.976
♪ Opening Song ♪

03:16.156 --> 03:17.946
[ANNIE] We have no choice
but to kill 'em all

03:18.026 --> 03:19.616
with our first strike.

03:19.696 --> 03:23.156
That's the only way we can
secure the flying boat.

03:23.246 --> 03:26.286
To pull this off,
everyone's gotta be in sync.

03:26.376 --> 03:31.296
We need our Titan power and
your firepower. Understood?

03:33.626 --> 03:35.046
Just hold on a second.

03:35.126 --> 03:36.716
What's the problem?

03:37.966 --> 03:40.636
The Jaegerists are holding
all the Azumabito hostage.

03:40.716 --> 03:42.306
We need to keep them
out of the line of fire.

03:42.386 --> 03:44.436
[CONNY gasps]
Yeah, exactly!

03:44.516 --> 03:46.596
You expect us to
care about that?

03:46.686 --> 03:48.606
We won't protect people
who've attacked our homeland

03:48.686 --> 03:50.476
just 'cause they're
your distant cousins.

03:50.566 --> 03:53.486
[PIECK] Slow down, Annie.
If the hostages are killed,

03:53.566 --> 03:56.656
the rest of the plan
falls apart.

03:56.736 --> 03:58.566
Right, Onyankopon?

03:58.656 --> 04:00.536
Yeah, we need him alive.

04:00.616 --> 04:02.326
I should be able to
pilot their boat,

04:02.406 --> 04:04.826
but first we gotta
get it into flying shape.

04:04.916 --> 04:06.116
That's the problem.

04:06.206 --> 04:08.166
We need the mechanics
to set up the wings.

04:08.246 --> 04:11.916
Otherwise, none of us are
gonna be flying anywhere.

04:11.996 --> 04:14.756
The wings are folded up
to make it easier to tow,

04:14.836 --> 04:17.086
so they'll need to be
extended and secured.

04:17.176 --> 04:19.136
And even then,
there's still more to do

04:19.216 --> 04:21.216
before we can get airborne.

04:22.386 --> 04:23.926
[ONYANKOPON] The original
plan was to hangar it

04:24.016 --> 04:25.226
'til we had some pilots trained,

04:25.306 --> 04:27.136
so we're skipping
a lot of steps,

04:27.226 --> 04:28.306
but they'll at least
need some time

04:28.396 --> 04:30.856
to service it before takeoff.

04:30.936 --> 04:34.396
Start to finish, how long
is it gonna take to service?

04:35.316 --> 04:39.616
I couldn't say.
It'll be up to the mechanics.

04:43.446 --> 04:45.956
I get it. But to confirm,

04:46.036 --> 04:48.706
you're asking us to protect
the Azumabito technicians

04:48.786 --> 04:52.456
from the Jaegerists long enough
to get the boat ready to fly.

04:52.546 --> 04:53.666
And let me guess.

04:53.746 --> 04:55.206
You want us to
hold the enemy off

04:55.296 --> 04:59.216
for this unknown length of time
without killing any of them.

05:01.966 --> 05:03.846
If at all possible.

05:03.926 --> 05:06.386
We've known these guys
ever since we were cadets.

05:06.476 --> 05:09.896
Then I'm sure you've got a plan.
Think you could fill me in?

05:09.976 --> 05:11.186
We don't even have
an estimate on

05:11.266 --> 05:13.646
how long the Azumabito
will need yet.

05:13.726 --> 05:15.356
So you must have some scheme to

05:15.436 --> 05:17.856
keep the Jaegerists
occupied indefinitely

05:17.946 --> 05:19.276
without killing them.

05:19.356 --> 05:22.276
Can you explain it in detail?

05:22.366 --> 05:25.156
There is a plan, right, Armin?

05:25.246 --> 05:27.156
You had one for me.

05:30.746 --> 05:33.046
There's no way
to make that happen.

05:33.126 --> 05:35.586
We have to wipe them out
with a lightning strike,

05:35.666 --> 05:38.836
or else a survivor will destroy
the boat and strand us here.

05:40.836 --> 05:43.176
[CONNY] Hold on! We can see
that it's a long shot,

05:43.256 --> 05:45.096
but we're doing this
to help people!

05:45.176 --> 05:47.096
So what? You're saying
we have to gun down

05:47.176 --> 05:49.806
a bunch of our friends
to save the world?

05:49.886 --> 05:51.556
That's so messed up!

05:56.186 --> 05:59.896
[ANNIE] I'm sorry. This'll be
a pretty ugly operation.

05:59.986 --> 06:03.486
We shouldn't expect
you guys to take part in it.

06:03.566 --> 06:06.826
We don't even have the right
to drop that choice on you.

06:08.656 --> 06:10.456
If it had been you in our place,

06:10.536 --> 06:12.126
you probably would have
chosen differently

06:12.206 --> 06:13.666
than we did that day.

06:13.746 --> 06:15.416
You wouldn't have
breached the wall.

06:15.496 --> 06:16.626
[Gasps]

06:16.706 --> 06:18.836
Turns out that I was right.

06:18.916 --> 06:20.966
I am the same as you.

06:21.046 --> 06:25.006
[REINER]
Is that what he was saying?

06:27.846 --> 06:30.016
[REINER] None of you
need to join this battle.

06:31.136 --> 06:32.936
[REINER]
Stick with Gabi and Falco.

06:33.016 --> 06:35.646
Stay at a safe distance
and observe.

06:35.726 --> 06:37.066
You'll have to defend yourselves

06:37.146 --> 06:40.486
if the Jaegerists spot you,
so be prepared to fight.

06:40.566 --> 06:43.816
But for now,
just stay out of it.

06:46.786 --> 06:50.446
And let you guys kill each other
while we sit back and watch?

06:50.536 --> 06:51.746
Would that work?

06:51.826 --> 06:52.996
Can Titans even win this

06:53.076 --> 06:55.576
without infantry
backing them up?

06:57.296 --> 06:58.626
[Gasps]

06:58.706 --> 07:00.966
[HANGE] I've got no intention
of being a spectator.

07:01.046 --> 07:03.256
Look. I know they
were our comrades,

07:03.336 --> 07:05.586
but I've already
had to shoot four.

07:05.676 --> 07:08.426
On top of that, our window
for saving humanity

07:08.506 --> 07:10.766
is shorter than we realized.

07:10.846 --> 07:13.056
I saw the Titans
crossing the sea,

07:13.136 --> 07:16.146
leaving monstrous clouds
of steam in their wake,

07:16.226 --> 07:18.396
and considering how fast
they were moving,

07:18.476 --> 07:22.396
they've probably made
landfall in Marley by now.

07:22.486 --> 07:24.986
The closest cities in
Northeastern Marley

07:25.066 --> 07:27.486
are most likely gone.

07:27.576 --> 07:29.076
I had no idea
they would be able to

07:29.156 --> 07:32.246
make it across
the sea that quickly.

07:32.326 --> 07:35.666
There's no telling how many
people they've already killed.

07:41.706 --> 07:44.626
Tell us where Eren Jaeger
is going with those Titans!

07:44.716 --> 07:50.136
[MAGATH grunting]

07:50.216 --> 07:52.056
Every time you make me
ask you again,

07:52.136 --> 07:55.346
I'll break you a new elbow!

07:55.436 --> 07:56.186
[MAGATH grunts]

07:56.266 --> 07:57.516
[YELENA screams]

07:57.606 --> 08:00.186
[MAGATH grunts]

08:00.266 --> 08:02.106
[HANGE]
Magath, stop it!

08:03.146 --> 08:04.486
[gasps]

08:04.566 --> 08:07.986
Why do you look so damn afraid?
I'm not gonna kill you.

08:10.486 --> 08:12.786
That's certainly good to hear.

08:12.866 --> 08:14.666
I've changed my mind.

08:14.746 --> 08:16.206
Now that you've
caught me up in this,

08:16.286 --> 08:19.086
I don't wanna die without
knowing how it ends.

08:19.166 --> 08:23.126
If we survive,
and you take me with you,

08:23.206 --> 08:26.546
I might tell you
where to find Eren.

08:26.636 --> 08:28.836
Securing that boat
is priority one.

08:28.926 --> 08:32.216
Yeah. Torturing her isn't
gonna do us any good now.

08:50.156 --> 08:52.826
Forgive me. All of you.

08:52.906 --> 08:56.076
I was a fool.

08:56.156 --> 08:59.206
I'm sorry for
my behavior last night.

08:59.286 --> 09:03.006
We were never in the right.

09:03.086 --> 09:06.216
I'd deluded myself into thinking
we were the good guys.

09:06.296 --> 09:07.926
I wanted to believe
the evil I'd done

09:08.006 --> 09:10.386
was justified as part of
some great cause.

09:10.466 --> 09:13.216
But in the end,
that's just not true.

09:13.306 --> 09:14.846
I'd attempted to
ignore the fact that

09:14.926 --> 09:16.886
Marley's soul has grown rotten,

09:16.976 --> 09:20.686
as I didn't want to consider
what that said about me.

09:20.766 --> 09:22.936
This war isn't your fault.

09:23.026 --> 09:24.936
You shouldn't be punished
for the sins of people

09:25.026 --> 09:28.946
you never knew simply because
their blood flows in your veins.

09:31.906 --> 09:35.616
[MAGATH]
Pieck. Annie. Reiner.

09:35.696 --> 09:38.116
You've been shouldering the
burden of humanity's hatred

09:38.206 --> 09:41.626
since you were born.
It's inexcusable.

09:41.706 --> 09:43.206
But still.

09:43.296 --> 09:45.416
Senseless as our
bloodstained history may be,

09:45.506 --> 09:47.466
we have a duty to pass it on,

09:47.546 --> 09:51.426
so the generations
after us can do better.

09:51.506 --> 09:53.386
Jaeger plans to
erase everything,

09:53.466 --> 09:55.596
including the lessons
of the past.

09:55.676 --> 09:57.636
And I call that unforgivable.

09:57.726 --> 09:59.686
As long as this wanton
killing continues,

09:59.766 --> 10:02.096
our world will only
sink deeper into hell.

10:02.186 --> 10:04.186
We have to break the cycle!

10:05.066 --> 10:06.146
[BOTH gasp]

10:06.226 --> 10:09.606
But right now,
we're trapped in it.

10:09.696 --> 10:12.816
There's no way to avoid
spilling more blood today.

10:12.906 --> 10:16.536
So please, look the other way.

10:24.996 --> 10:26.956
[ARMIN]
I'm not doing that.

10:29.256 --> 10:32.886
I refuse to let someone else
stain their hands in my place.

10:46.106 --> 10:49.686
[FLOCH] Look at the size
of those steam clouds.

10:49.776 --> 10:53.026
History has never changed
so much in a single day!

10:53.986 --> 10:57.906
[FLOCH] Of course, the history
of Hizuru will change as well.

10:57.986 --> 11:01.036
All of civilization is
about to be flattened,

11:01.116 --> 11:04.496
and something new
will arise where it stood.

11:04.576 --> 11:07.796
Whatever concerns you had
will soon be dead and gone.

11:07.876 --> 11:10.206
We have only the future
to worry about,

11:10.296 --> 11:13.256
so focus on what you can
contribute to the island.

11:13.336 --> 11:15.506
These gentlemen, for instance.

11:15.586 --> 11:17.056
Hizuru's brightest
engineers will be

11:17.136 --> 11:22.016
a valuable asset to
our homeland. Right?

11:22.096 --> 11:24.846
It would be a shame to
have to lose any more of them,

11:24.936 --> 11:27.396
so please kindly
do as you're told.

11:29.476 --> 11:31.356
I was hoping I could
avoid saying anything

11:31.436 --> 11:33.276
that would disrupt
this fine mood you're in.

11:33.356 --> 11:34.356
Huh?

11:34.446 --> 11:35.986
But what is this change
you speak of,

11:36.066 --> 11:38.446
and what good do you
think would come of it?

11:39.366 --> 11:41.246
If you believe slaughtering
the human race

11:41.326 --> 11:43.616
will guarantee peace
here on Paradis,

11:43.706 --> 11:45.786
you'll be quite disappointed.

11:47.246 --> 11:48.996
You won't make your world
any less violent

11:49.086 --> 11:50.956
by making it smaller.

11:51.046 --> 11:52.756
When tomorrow comes,
you'll have accomplished

11:52.836 --> 11:56.136
nothing more than containing
the killing to your own home.

11:59.766 --> 12:01.926
I'll take your words to heart.

12:02.016 --> 12:05.516
In fact, I've been approaching
the same conclusion.

12:05.596 --> 12:09.856
But in any world, it's important
to understand our place.

12:12.396 --> 12:15.156
Hizuru's technology
would be useful to Eldia,

12:15.236 --> 12:17.446
but our security's
our greatest concern,

12:17.526 --> 12:18.776
and we don't need a flying boat

12:18.866 --> 12:21.986
or a seafaring fleet to
move forward as a nation.

12:22.076 --> 12:25.166
Trouble will be
nipped in the bud. Got it?

12:25.246 --> 12:27.456
This is the world now.

12:27.536 --> 12:32.956
You need to recognize your place
in it. Do you understand?

12:33.046 --> 12:36.216
[ARMIN]
Floch! Where are you?

12:36.296 --> 12:38.586
We need the Azumabito!

12:38.676 --> 12:39.966
Wait, Armin?

12:40.056 --> 12:41.176
[ARMIN]
There you are!

12:41.256 --> 12:42.596
[FLOCH]
What are you yelling for?

12:42.676 --> 12:44.266
Where have you been?

12:44.346 --> 12:46.396
[ARMIN]
I was following the Cart Titan!

12:46.476 --> 12:48.346
It regrouped with
the Armored Titan.

12:48.436 --> 12:50.226
They're escaping
together by sea!

12:50.316 --> 12:52.146
We can't let them
catch up with Eren!

12:52.226 --> 12:54.186
We need that
flying boat airborne!

12:54.276 --> 12:57.566
Tell the Azumabito mechanics
to get it ready, right now!

13:01.326 --> 13:02.736
What are you telling me, Armin?

13:02.826 --> 13:04.616
Why didn't you
chase after the Cart?

13:04.696 --> 13:06.746
If you had,
this would be over by now!

13:06.826 --> 13:09.166
It was obvious that
they were gonna head south!

13:09.246 --> 13:10.576
Now we've lost them.

13:10.666 --> 13:13.086
You know they killed Jean
and Onyonkopon, right?

13:13.166 --> 13:16.376
[CONNY] Armin!
The flying boat's over here!

13:17.716 --> 13:20.086
[ARMIN] Floch! Get the
Azumabito mechanics

13:20.176 --> 13:22.136
down here right away!

13:33.776 --> 13:36.106
--Hold on!
--Stop right there!

13:36.186 --> 13:38.986
[CONNY] Daz? Samuel?
What are you doing?

13:40.946 --> 13:44.116
[CONNY gasps]
Are those explosives?

13:45.576 --> 13:47.116
[ARMIN]
Get 'em off the boat already!

13:47.196 --> 13:49.116
[CONNY] Hurry up, we gotta
get this thing ready to launch!

13:49.206 --> 13:50.746
The Marleyans are
gonna get away!

13:50.826 --> 13:52.996
--[DAZ] Easy!
--[SAMUEL] Settle down, okay?

13:53.086 --> 13:54.756
We need to talk first.

13:54.836 --> 13:57.376
There have been rumors
going around since yesterday.

13:57.466 --> 13:59.126
People say you guys
teamed up with Marley,

13:59.216 --> 14:00.546
and that you plan to
use the flying boat

14:00.636 --> 14:02.426
to stop the rumbling.

14:02.506 --> 14:03.846
That's not true, is it?

14:03.926 --> 14:05.806
[ARMIN gasps]

14:05.886 --> 14:08.806
What? What kinda
crazy talk is that?

14:08.886 --> 14:10.266
We're with you!

14:10.346 --> 14:12.806
Eren has to finish the job,
or this island is doomed!

14:12.896 --> 14:15.316
Yeah. That's what I thought.

14:15.396 --> 14:18.026
We've been fighting so long
to save our home.

14:18.106 --> 14:19.446
After all you've been through,

14:19.526 --> 14:22.446
I knew there was no way you'd
put us in danger again.

14:23.526 --> 14:24.946
Yeah, you're damn right,
there's not!

14:25.036 --> 14:26.786
That's a relief.

14:26.866 --> 14:28.536
If you'd actually
turned your backs on us,

14:28.616 --> 14:30.956
I can't even imagine
what I would have done.

14:31.036 --> 14:34.916
[ARMIN] But we didn't, Daz.
Now, the explosives, please?

14:43.506 --> 14:44.966
[DAZ]
I know you get that Eren's doing

14:45.056 --> 14:47.266
what's necessary to protect us.

14:47.346 --> 14:48.636
But a part of me still
thought you might

14:48.716 --> 14:51.846
side with the enemy
and try to stop him.

15:02.856 --> 15:06.406
[Gasps] What's wrong, guys?

15:06.486 --> 15:08.736
I disconnected the detonator.

15:10.536 --> 15:11.706
[ARMIN]
That's done.

15:11.786 --> 15:13.326
Now we have to hope
Floch listens to me

15:13.416 --> 15:15.996
and sends out the
Azumabito mechanics.

15:16.916 --> 15:18.376
[ARMIN]
If we can get the boat ready,

15:18.456 --> 15:22.506
all we'll need is a way to get
our team aboard, and it's over.

15:22.586 --> 15:24.716
There's a chance
we can pull this off

15:24.796 --> 15:27.756
and stop Eren without
any more killing.

15:34.686 --> 15:36.476
[FLOCH]
Think about it.

15:36.566 --> 15:39.226
It doesn't quite
add up, does it?

15:40.896 --> 15:42.236
Armin said it was obvious that

15:42.316 --> 15:44.526
the enemy would
flee to the south,

15:44.606 --> 15:47.526
but the locomotive is
the fastest way here.

15:48.786 --> 15:51.076
[FLOCH] Instead,
they pursued on horseback,

15:51.156 --> 15:53.576
even though the Cart
already had a head start.

15:53.666 --> 15:55.956
[sighs] What have
they been up to

15:56.036 --> 15:58.496
since they went incommunicado?

15:58.586 --> 16:02.006
Truth is, there's no
proof of anything.

16:02.086 --> 16:05.926
Still, my gut tells me
this is trouble.

16:06.006 --> 16:08.096
So it's time to nip some buds.

16:08.176 --> 16:09.596
[ALL gasp]

16:12.346 --> 16:14.436
[Gunshots]

16:21.936 --> 16:23.606
[ARMIN]
We failed!

16:25.696 --> 16:27.406
--[JAEGERIST 85A] Hey!
--[JAEGERIST 85B] Floch!

16:28.776 --> 16:32.446
Idiots! Quit staring
and blow her away!

16:32.536 --> 16:35.076
Did you think I'd
go down without a fight?

16:38.036 --> 16:39.706
[MIKASA grunts]

16:40.546 --> 16:42.506
Kiyomi, run!

16:42.586 --> 16:45.006
[Yells]

16:47.386 --> 16:48.506
We're under attack!

16:48.586 --> 16:50.636
Mikasa, Armin, and Conny
have switched sides!

16:50.716 --> 16:55.556
They've betrayed
Eldia! Kill them!

16:57.686 --> 17:01.646
[MIKASA gasps] They're gonna
fire through the windows!

17:04.646 --> 17:06.486
Get down to the basement!

17:08.356 --> 17:09.776
[Gasps]

17:13.326 --> 17:15.406
[MIKASA]
It's a firefight now.

17:15.496 --> 17:16.996
The only way through

17:17.076 --> 17:19.326
is to wipe out
every last Jaegerist!

17:19.416 --> 17:21.206
[KIYOMI]
Lady Mikasa!

17:23.756 --> 17:25.336
[MIKASA yells]

17:27.676 --> 17:29.586
[MAGATH]
This way, all of you!

17:29.676 --> 17:31.756
We can hunker down
in the basement!

17:31.846 --> 17:34.386
If you wanna stay alive,
then come with me!

17:46.316 --> 17:47.276
Hold on!

17:47.356 --> 17:49.316
Wait, Daz! What are
you trying to--

17:52.866 --> 17:55.156
--Armin!
--[SAMUEL] Don't move!

17:58.656 --> 18:00.036
[CONNY]
Samuel.

18:03.626 --> 18:04.796
Don't stop.

18:04.876 --> 18:07.836
Reconnect the detonator
and blow up the boat.

18:07.916 --> 18:09.506
Hurry up, Daz!

18:12.926 --> 18:15.596
[CONNY]
Samuel? Hey.

18:15.676 --> 18:18.306
[SAMUEL] You said we'd
eat meat together, Conny.

18:18.386 --> 18:21.096
And we finally could've
made that happen.

18:21.186 --> 18:24.186
We've got room
to raise livestock,

18:24.266 --> 18:26.436
just like we imagined it!

18:29.566 --> 18:33.196
[SAMUEL] Dammit all to hell.
How did it end up like this?

18:41.786 --> 18:44.336
The only way out of here
is through the enemy!

18:44.416 --> 18:46.336
We'll be overrun
as soon as they regroup!

18:46.416 --> 18:49.086
We'll be fine!
As long as we're down here,

18:49.166 --> 18:50.626
we'll be safe when
our reinforcements

18:50.716 --> 18:53.466
jump into the fray
up on the surface!

18:53.546 --> 18:54.966
Enemy in the basement!

18:55.056 --> 18:57.386
Follow me and
bring more explosives!

19:06.776 --> 19:09.526
[FLOCH] Why would they
back themselves into a corner?

19:18.076 --> 19:21.326
[FLOCH]
No. They didn't!

19:29.966 --> 19:30.716
[Gasps]

19:30.796 --> 19:31.916
[CONNY yells]

19:33.876 --> 19:39.466
[ONYANKOPON] The plan failed.
Why does it always end this way?

19:40.726 --> 19:44.976
Violence will always be
a part of human existence,

19:45.056 --> 19:47.646
won't it, Captain?

20:02.456 --> 20:04.166
[JAEGERISTS gasp]

20:04.246 --> 20:07.376
[JAEGERISTS scream]

20:21.766 --> 20:24.136
[JAEGERIST 85O] We need to
get more Thunder Spears!

20:25.306 --> 20:26.806
No, no, no!

20:41.906 --> 20:43.496
You have to blow up
the boat, Daz!

20:43.576 --> 20:44.746
[Gasps]

20:53.506 --> 20:55.166
Stop, Armin!

20:56.796 --> 20:58.586
Get off me!

21:03.306 --> 21:06.266
[DAZ]
I don't wanna do this!

21:06.346 --> 21:07.226
Armin!

21:07.306 --> 21:08.976
Why are you betraying us?

21:09.056 --> 21:11.016
I don't understand, Conny!

21:11.106 --> 21:14.526
We were supposed to be on
the same side, no matter what!

21:14.606 --> 21:18.856
We still are on
the same side, Samuel!

21:18.946 --> 21:22.326
But I-- I just--!

21:33.796 --> 21:36.376
One of you is gonna have to
be the one to do it.

21:36.466 --> 21:42.346
[CONNY yelling]

21:42.426 --> 21:45.676
[CONNY yelling]

21:51.726 --> 21:52.976
Wait, Conny--

21:55.276 --> 21:59.656
[BERTHOLDT] One of you has to
stain your hands with my blood!

22:01.526 --> 22:06.956
[CONNY screams]

22:09.956 --> 22:14.956
♪ Ending Song ♪

23:41.296 --> 23:43.216
[NARRATOR]
Hesitation is death.

23:43.296 --> 23:46.176
Aim the gun and
pull the trigger,

23:46.256 --> 23:48.516
and know that
with your betrayal,

23:48.596 --> 23:51.976
the world might live
to see another day.

23:52.056 --> 23:54.936
Next episode: "Retrospective."
